{
  "dom_id": "step-136780",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Transitive Relations Defined On Infinite Sets",
  "problem": "Which of the following relations are transitive? \n\n- $x \\: R \\: y$ if and only if $x \\not\\mid y,$ defined on $\\mathbb{Z}$\n\n- $x \\: S \\: y$ if and only if $x = y,$ defined on $\\mathbb{R}$\n\n- $x \\: T \\: y$ if and only if $6 \\mid (x+y),$ defined on $\\mathbb{Z}$",
  "worked_solution": "A binary relation $R$ defined on a set $A$ is *transitive* if, for all $x,y,z \\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y) \\in R \\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad (y,z) \\in R \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\quad (x,z) \\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if the pairs $(x,y)$ and $(y,z)$ belong to a transitive relation, then the pair $(x,z)$ should also be in the relation.\n\nIt's sufficient to check all the \"linked\" pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x \\neq y$ and $(y,z)$ with $y \\neq z.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our relations.\n\n- Relation $R$ is not transitive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,3) \\in R$ since $2 \\not\\mid 3,$ and\n\n- $(3,4) \\in R$ since $3 \\not\\mid 4,$ but\n\n- $(2,4) \\notin R$ since $2 \\mid 4.$\n\n- Relation $S$ is transitive. Indeed, if $(x,y) \\in S$ and $(y,x) \\in S,$ then $(x,z) \\in S.$ Notice that \n\n$$\nx = y \\quad\\textrm{and}\\quad y = z \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad x = z\n$$\n\nfor all $x,y,z \\in \\mathbb{R}.$\n\n- Relation $T$ is not transitive. Notice that \n\n- $(2,4) \\in T$ since $6 \\mid (2+4),$ and\n\n- $(4,8) \\in T$ since $6 \\mid (4+8),$ but\n\n- $(2,8) \\notin T$ since $6 \\not\\mid (2+8).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$S$ only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-136780\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"136780\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"14667\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-136780\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-13\">Transitive Relations Defined On Infinite Sets</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"136780\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                